(* A held Sequence spliced under HoldFirst can move its parts into an unheld position, where the next round evaluates them (wolfram/HoldFirst/PropertiesAndRelations/5). One that an unheld argument evaluated to shifts what follows it without releasing it: under HoldRest, g[Sequence[], 1+1, 2+2] stays g[1+1, 2+2] in WL 15.0.1 (0080). Under HoldAll nothing moves out of hold. *)
SetAttributes[f, HoldFirst]
f[Sequence[Plus[1, 1], Plus[2, 2]], Plus[3, 3]]
SetAttributes[g, HoldRest]
g[Plus[1, 1], Sequence[Plus[1, 1], Plus[2, 2]]]
g[Sequence[], Plus[1, 1], Plus[2, 2]]
Hold[Sequence[Plus[1, 1], Plus[2, 2]], Plus[3, 3]]
